const faq = [
  ['How much water does a lawn need per week?', 'About an inch a week from rain and watering combined in summer, a bit less in spring and fall. Less when it’s cool and cloudy, more in a heat wave. The rain meter does this math for you from real rain and the forecast.'],
  ['How do I know if my lawn needs water?', 'Walk on it. If your footprints stay pressed down instead of springing back, or the grass turns a dull blue-gray, it’s thirsty. Another test: a screwdriver should slide into the soil easily.'],
  ['What time of day should I water my lawn?', 'Early morning, before about 9am. Less water evaporates, and the grass dries off during the day, which keeps disease down. Watering at night leaves it wet for hours.'],
  ['Should I water every day?', 'No. Water deep and less often, about once or twice a week, so roots grow down. A little bit every day keeps roots shallow and invites crabgrass and disease. New seed is the exception.'],
  ['Is it OK to let my lawn go brown in summer?', 'Yes. Cool-season grass goes dormant in heat and drought to protect itself, and usually greens up a couple of weeks after real rain. Just don’t switch back and forth between watering and not. Pick one.'],
];
const sources = [
